# Lab 3: Authentication and Authorization
# Create tokens from the project folder (src/Ticketing.Api), then paste them below:
#   dotnet user-jwts create --name alice --role requester
#   dotnet user-jwts create --name bob --role requester
#   dotnet user-jwts create --name dana --role agent
@host = https://localhost:7001
@ticketId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@alice = paste-alice-token-here
@bob = paste-bob-token-here
@dana = paste-dana-token-here
# The API key comes from appsettings.Development.json (Step 6)
@apiKey = dev-ops-dashboard-key-change-me

### 401: no token
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets

### alice lists tickets: only hers
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### dana (agent) lists tickets: all of them
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{dana}}

### alice reads her own ticket: 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### bob reads alice's ticket: 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}

### bob creates a ticket for himself: 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "My laptop", "description": "Won't boot.", "priority": "High", "requesterId": "bob" }

### bob creates a ticket as alice: 403
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Framing alice", "description": "Hmm.", "priority": "Low", "requesterId": "alice" }

### alice tries to close her own ticket: 403 (agents only)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### dana assigns it to herself: 200
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{dana}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assigneeId": "dana" }

### A service caller with an API key (no bearer token)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### A wrong API key: 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
X-Api-Key: guessed-key
